# zig-only
# `Ctrl-A` / `Ctrl-X` know Neovim's default `nrformats=bin,hex`: `0x0f`
# becomes `0x10` (the letter case kept), `0b101` becomes `0b110`, and
# a zero-padded decimal keeps its width — `007` `Ctrl-X` is `006`,
# `000` `Ctrl-X` is `-001` (`:help CTRL-A`).
write a.txt "hex 0x0f oct 007 pad 000 bin 0b101 up 0xFF\n"
open a.txt
command editor.use_vim

key ctrl+a
type fo
key ctrl+x
type fp
key ctrl+x
type fb
key ctrl+a
type fu
key ctrl+a
command file.save
expect file a.txt contains "hex 0x10 oct 006 pad -001 bin 0b110 up 0x100\n"
type 0
type 3
key ctrl+x
command file.save
expect file a.txt contains "hex 0x0d oct"
